Use this guide to create a spreadsheet of pupil data for the vaccination team.

This guide is for school office staff and MIS managers who use Bromcom.

> You need reporting permissions. These are set in **Config**, then **Setup**, then **Roles &amp; Permissions**. If you do not have them, ask your MIS manager.

## Export pupil data

1. Go to **Modules**, then **Reporting**, then **Reports**, then **Create New Report**, then **Quick Report**.
2. Choose **Student** as the data source.
3. Add a name, then drag the data items you need into the **Report Layout**.
4. Filter by the school you’re providing information for.
5. Filter by the year groups you’re providing information for.
6. Select **Save**, then **Run Report**.
7. Go to **Actions**, then **Export**, then select **CSV**.

## Select the school

If you use Bromcom for one school, skip this step. Your report will only include pupils at that school.

If you use a trust-wide or federated view:

1. Use the school selector at the top of the page to switch to the school you’re providing information for.
2. Or go to **Filters**, select **School**, then select the school you’re providing information for.
3. Select **Apply**.

## Select the year groups

1. Go to **Filters**, select **Year Group**, then select **Add filter**.
2. Select the year groups you’re providing information for.
3. Check that **Status** is set to **On Roll**, then select **Apply**.

